 a Japanese input source\nL60:     * cite25†Set up the input source L61:     * cite26†Switch the input source L62:     * cite27†Edit and use your user dictionaries L63:     * Enter characters\nL64:       * cite28†Enter Japanese text L65:       * cite29†Enter characters using the Kana Table L66:       * cite30†Enter full-width or half-width numbers L67:       * cite31†Enter symbols L68:       * cite32†Change characters you entered L69:       * cite33†Use the candidate window L70:       * cite34†Type roman strings using hiragana or katakana L71:       * cite35†Roman characters and corresponding kana L72:     * Convert characters\nL73:       * cite36†Improve conversion accuracy L74:       * cite37†Convert hiragana numbers into other notations L75:       * cite38†Convert text using a punctuation mark L76:       * cite39†Insert and convert characters between characters L77:       * cite40†Reverse a conversion L78:       * cite41†Keyboard shortcuts L79:     * cite42†Change Japanese settings L80:   * Use the Ainu input source\nL81:     * cite43†Set up and switch to the Ainu input source L82:     * cite44†Look up roman/kana character correlation L83:   * cite45†Choose a sort order for lists in Japanese L84:   * cite46†Copyright and trademarks L85: cite47†Image†help.apple.com L86: # Keyboard shortcuts for Japanese conversions on Mac\nL87: \nL88: After you cite48†set up a Japanese input source , you can use the keyboard shortcuts shown in the tables below to convert characters while using any one of the Japanese input sources.\nL89: \nL90: For keyboard shortcuts you can use to switch from one input source to another, see cite49†Switch to a Japanese input source .\nL91: Note: Keyboard shortcuts in apps may vary depending on the language and keyboard layout you’re using on your Mac. If the shortcuts below don’t work as you expect, look in the app menus in the menu bar to see the correct shortcuts. You can also cite50†use the Keyboard Viewer to see your current keyboard layout, known as an input source.\nL92: ## Convert from one input source to another\nL93: \nL94:   1. On your Mac, cite49†switch to a Japanese input source .\nL95: \nL96:   2. In an app, cite51†enter text .\nL97: \nL98:   3. Use the keyboard shortcuts shown in the table below to convert characters to different input modes. If the shortcut contains a function key, such as F8, you may need to also press the Fn key; for example, press Fn-F8.\nL99: Action  | Keyboard shortcut\nL100: --- | ---\nL101: Convert characters to hiragana  | Control-J or F6\nL102: Convert characters to katakana  | Control-K or F7\nL103: Convert characters to full-width romaji  | Control-L or F9\nL104: Convert characters to romaji (the default)  | Control-Semicolon (;) or F8\nL105: Convert characters to half-width katakana(in Japanese – Kana or Japanese – Romaji Input Sources settings only if Half-width Katakana is selected)  | Control-Semicolon (;) or F8\nL106: Convert characters to romaji  | Control-Colon (:) or F10\nL107: Convert characters to romaji(with ANSI keyboard selected)  | Control-Apostrophe (')\nL108: ## Convert kana to kanji\nL109: \nL110:   1. On your Mac, cite49†switch to a Japanese input source .\nL111: \nL112:   2. In an app, cite51†enter text .\nL113: \nL114:   3. Use the keyboard shortcuts shown in the table below to convert kana to kanji.\nL115: \nL116: When selecting segments of a conversion, a bold underline indicates the selection.\nL117: \nL118: Note: When writing horizontally, use the arrow keys in the keyboard shortcuts below. When writing vertically, use the other set of arrow keys instead. For example, the Left Arrow key instead of the Down Arrow key.\nL119: Action  | Mac keyboard shortcut  | Windows-style keyboard shortcut\nL120: --- | --- | ---\nL121: Convert to kanji  | Space bar  | Space bar\nL122: Select the next kanji candidate  | Down Arrow key Space bar Control-N  | Down Arrow key Space bar\nL123: Select the previous kanji candidate  | Up Arrow key Shift-Space bar Control-P  | Up Arrow key Shift-Space bar\nL124: Jump through 8 candidate rows  | Shift-Up Arrow or Down Arrow key Control-V Control-R  | Shift-Left Arrow or Right Arrow key Page Up key or Page Down key\nL125: Revert back to yomi while still selecting a kanji (before conversion)  | Escape key  | Escape key Control-Z\nL126: Confirm kanji conversion  | Return  | Return\nL127: Display alternate kanji candidates for already converted text  | Control-Shift-R Option-Shift-R Press the Kana key twice  | Control-Shift-R Alt-Shift-R Press the Kana key twice\nL128: Select the next segment of a conversion (a bold underline indicates the selection)  | Up Arrow key Control-B  | Up Arrow key\nL129: Select the previous segment of a conversion (a bold underline indicates the selection)  | Down Arrow key Control-F  | Down Arrow key\nL130: Expand the selected segment  | Shift-Right Arrow key Control-W Control-O  | Shift-Right Arrow key Control-L\nL131: Decrease the selected segment  | Shift-Left Arrow key Control-I  | Shift-Left Arrow key Control-K\nL132: Move cursor up  | Up Arrow key Control-E  | Left Arrow key Control-E\nL133: Move cursor down  | Down Arrow key Control-X  | Right Arrow key Control-X\nL134: Move cursor left  | Left Arrow key Control-S  | Left Arrow key Control-S\nL135: Move cursor right  | Right Arrow key Control-D  | Right Arrow key Control-D\nL136: Delete character backwards  | Delete key Control-H  | Delete key Control-H\nL137: Delete all text that is considered for conversion  | Escape key Clear key  | Escape key\nL138: Undo conversion  | Control-Delete key Press the Kana key twice  | Control-Delete key Press the Kana key twice\nL139: Convert Eiji (western characters) to kana  | Press the Kana key twice  | Press the Kana key twice\nL140: Convert kana to Eiji (western characters)  | Press the Eisu Alphanumeric key twice  | Press the Eisu Alphanumeric key twice\nL141: See alsoc